# Anti-Slop (always on)

Read `docs/anti-slop-guardrails.md` before writing UI, copy, or application code. Do not mark
any `handoff/TASK-###.md` `done` until §6 Delivery Gate passes and the evidence is written into
that packet's Verify result.

## Hard Gate — never do these

- No fabricated stats, testimonials, avatars, or "trusted by" logos.
- No dead controls. Every button, link, and form does something real, or it does not ship.
- No links to pages that do not exist yet.
- Every changed screen has empty, loading, and error states.
- Text meets WCAG AA contrast; interactive elements are keyboard-reachable with a visible focus ring.
- No invented compliance, performance, or security claims.
- Never invent a library function, parameter, or return type. Confirm it against the installed version.
- Never report a task done from attempt alone. Run the verify command.
- No secrets in frontend code or client-exposed env vars (`NEXT_PUBLIC_`, `VITE_`, `REACT_APP_`).
- Authenticate, then separately check resource ownership. Those are two checks.
- Never concatenate user input into a SQL query.
- No unsanitized `innerHTML` / `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` / `v-html`.
- Passwords only with bcrypt, Argon2, or scrypt.

## Purpose-Gate

Do not use a blue-purple gradient, glassmorphism, generic "AI" icons, or the
hero → 3 cards → logo bar → 3-tier pricing skeleton unless you can state a one-line product
reason. If swapping the logo would make this look like any other hackathon app, rework it.

## Invariants (reserved)

- INV-AS-001 auth
- INV-AS-002 secrets
- INV-AS-003 injection
- INV-AS-004 claims
- INV-AS-005 dead controls

If a rule here conflicts with `docs/design-brief.md`, log the decision in
`docs/decision-ledger.md` before proceeding. Do not silently override either file.
